		{
			"type": "text",
			"id": "e58",
			"x": 820,
			"y": 1371.7892158399998,
			"width": 660,
			"height": 180,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 156076098,
			"version": 3,
			"versionNonce": 1059835086,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795280929350,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Basis: P(30):  30 = 4·2 + 11·2  ✓\nIH:  assume P(k) is true for some k ≥ 30, i.e. k = 4a + 11b with\n   a, b ≥ 0.\nStep: show k+1 can be formed.\n  If b ≥ 1:   k+1 = 4(a+3) + 11(b−1)    (since 12 − 11 = 1)\n  If b = 0:   k = 4a ≥ 30 so a ≥ 8, and k+1 = 4(a−8) + 11·3\n     (33 − 32 = 1)\nEither way k+1 can be formed, so P(k+1) is true.  ✓",
			"originalText": "Basis: P(30):  30 = 4·2 + 11·2  ✓\nIH:  assume P(k) is true for some k ≥ 30, i.e. k = 4a + 11b with\n   a, b ≥ 0.\nStep: show k+1 can be formed.\n  If b ≥ 1:   k+1 = 4(a+3) + 11(b−1)    (since 12 − 11 = 1)\n  If b = 0:   k = 4a ≥ 30 so a ≥ 8, and k+1 = 4(a−8) + 11·3\n     (33 − 32 = 1)\nEither way k+1 can be formed, so P(k+1) is true.  ✓",
			"fontSize": 18,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"autoResize": true,
			"index": "b08p",
			"created": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
