		},
		{
			"type": "text",
			"id": "e67",
			"x": 820,
			"y": 2399.546751679999,
			"width": 660,
			"height": 247.5,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 932716638,
			"version": 3,
			"versionNonce": 552441362,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795280929350,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "P(n): √2 ≠ n/b for every positive integer b.\nBasis P(1): √2 > 1 ≥ 1/b for all b, so √2 ≠ 1/b.  ✓\nIH:  P(j) is true for all 1 ≤ j ≤ k.\nStep: suppose, for contradiction, √2 = (k+1)/b. Then 2b² =\n   (k+1)².\n  So (k+1)² is even, hence k+1 is even: k+1 = 2m.\n  Then 2b² = 4m², so b² = 2m², b is even: b = 2c.\n  Then √2 = 2m/2c = m/c, with 1 ≤ m = (k+1)/2 ≤ k.\n  This contradicts P(m), which is true by the IH.\nSo P(k+1) is true. Hence √2 ≠ n/b for all positive n, b,\nso √2 is irrational.  ✓",
			"originalText": "P(n): √2 ≠ n/b for every positive integer b.\nBasis P(1): √2 > 1 ≥ 1/b for all b, so √2 ≠ 1/b.  ✓\nIH:  P(j) is true for all 1 ≤ j ≤ k.\nStep: suppose, for contradiction, √2 = (k+1)/b. Then 2b² =\n   (k+1)².\n  So (k+1)² is even, hence k+1 is even: k+1 = 2m.\n  Then 2b² = 4m², so b² = 2m², b is even: b = 2c.\n  Then √2 = 2m/2c = m/c, with 1 ≤ m = (k+1)/2 ≤ k.\n  This contradicts P(m), which is true by the IH.\nSo P(k+1) is true. Hence √2 ≠ n/b for all positive n, b,\nso √2 is irrational.  ✓",
			"fontSize": 18,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"autoResize": true,
			"index": "b08x",
			"created": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "",
			"labelPosition": null,
			"baseFontSize": null
		},
