			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795280929346,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "n = 1 gives F(1) = 1 + F(⌊1/2⌋) = 1 + F(0), but F(0) is not\n   defined\n(the domain is the positive integers), and this also clashes with\n   F(1) = 1.\nSo F is not well-defined.",
			"originalText": "n = 1 gives F(1) = 1 + F(⌊1/2⌋) = 1 + F(0), but F(0) is not\n   defined\n(the domain is the positive integers), and this also clashes with\n   F(1) = 1.\nSo F is not well-defined.",
			"fontSize": 18,
			"fontFamily": 1,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
